# GENIE.AI SLIM lock for the dataprep microservice (issue #2000).
#
# Same source tree, same behaviour — the SLIM variant only changes WHAT THE
# FINAL IMAGE INSTALLS. The fat lock (requirements-cpu.txt, inherited from
# OPEA v1.5's compiled lock — the dataprep module has no requirements.in)
# resolves `torch==2.13.0` to the CUDA/cu13 build (15 `nvidia-*` wheels +
# triton, ~3.2 GB compressed in the pip layer) and drags in the whole OPEA
# ecosystem: pyspark, openai-whisper, graspologic, moviepy, the
# `llama-index-*` tree, the `langchain-{milvus,elasticsearch,mariadb,
# opengauss,pinecone}` family — none of which the dataprep's runtime chain
# imports.
#
# The dataprep DOES have a local-model path: `genieai_dataprep_utils.py`
# builds a docling pipeline with `EasyOcrOptions` and picks the accelerator
# from `DOCLING_DEVICE` (default "cuda", falling back to CPU when no GPU is
# visible), and easyocr runs its detector through torch/torchvision. So torch
# stays — but CPU-only: the `+cpu` local build from the PyTorch CPU index, at
# the SAME version (2.13.0). OCR keeps working; only the device changes.
#
# EVERY version below is the version the FAT lock pins — the slim image must
# not drift from the fat one on anything but torch. The TRANSITIVE
# dependencies still float, and are hash-pinned in the compiled lock.
#
# RUNTIME IMPORT SET (what the service actually imports at boot):
#   comps/dataprep/src/utils.py (module level): aiofiles, aiohttp, cairosvg,
#     cv2, docx, docx2txt, fitz (pymupdf), numpy, pandas, pptx, pytesseract,
#     yaml, BeautifulSoup, langchain (LLMChain/PromptTemplate),
#     langchain_community.document_loaders / .llms
#   comps/dataprep/src/integrations/arangodb.py: openai, arango,
#     langchain_arangodb, langchain_core, langchain_experimental,
#     langchain_huggingface, langchain_openai, langchain_text_splitters
#   comps/dataprep/src/opea_dataprep_microservice.py: the non-arangodb
#     integration imports are COMMENTED OUT at build time (Dockerfile Step J),
#     so elasticsearch / mariadb / milvus / neo4j / opengauss / opensearch /
#     pgvect / pinecone / qdrant / redis / vdms bring nothing.
#   GENIE overlay: easyocr + docling (OCR pipeline), unstructured
#     (partition_pdf, imported lazily inside the function), rank_bm25,
#     numpy, pydantic, fastapi, aiohttp, httpx, huggingface-hub, arango,
#     openai, comps core (docarray, shortuuid, Pillow, pyyaml, otel,
#     prometheus-fastapi-instrumentator)
#
# Regenerate with (the CPU index FIRST, and `unsafe-best-match` because uv's
# default `first-index` stops at PyPI, where torch==2.13.0 IS the CUDA
# build, and never reaches the CPU index's 2.13.0+cpu):
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.11 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_31 \
#     --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu \
#     --extra-index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
#     --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \
#     requirements-slim.in -o requirements-slim.txt

